WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.570
Two people, each with the same
shuffled pile of numbered cards.

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.530
Who sorts theirs first?

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.150
The first swaps neighbouring
cards, again and again,

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.810
nudging them into order.

5
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.410
The second does something strange.

6
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.430
She splits the pile in
half, then each half,

7
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.750
again and again, until single
cards are scattered everywhere.

8
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.330
Why would a fast sort start by
chopping a list into pieces,

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.150
and making the mess bigger?

10
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.950
In this mission, you'll
meet the merge sort.

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.590
It splits the list into two
halves, then splits each half,

12
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.090
until every list holds one item.

13
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.710
Then you'll merge two piles back into one,

14
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.430
by comparing the first items of both.

15
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.360
Your mission: work out why
making the mess first pays off.
